Of course, this is entirely in the Grand Tradition of predictions regarding
the future, which are virtually assured to be wildly off the mark. 
Gibson's story "The Gernsbach Continuum" is a wry comment on this.

Flying cars?  Mile-high skyscrapers?  Intelligent computers?  One World
Goverment?

